# Superalloys — working list for EcoSuit-AS
**Ni-base · Co-base · Fe–Ni-base**
Belt metal is Fe–5–10Ni + Co traces. Anything with serious Cr, Al, Ti, Mo, W, Nb, Ta, Re is an alloyed grade, not a raw M-type pour.

---

## 1. Families

| Family | Matrix | Why it exists | Belt-honest path |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ni-base | FCC Ni + γ′ Ni₃(Al,Ti) and/or solid solution | Hot section, oxidation, creep | Need concentrated Ni + imported Cr/Al/Ti/Mo/Nb |
| Co-base | FCC Co + carbides | Hot corrosion, thermal fatigue, less γ′ | Co is in irons (~0.5%); still need Cr/W |
| Fe–Ni-base | FCC Fe–Ni | Cheaper, cryogenic to mid-heat | Closest to slagged meteoritic FeNi + Cr |

