## 8. Elements you must import (or separately extract)

To move A → B → C:

| Element | In typical iron meteorite | In 718 | Problem |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ni | 5–10% (taenite pockets higher) | ~52% | Concentrate or sort taenite |
| Cr | ppm–0.2% | ~19% | Import or silicate ore |
| Nb | ~none | ~5% | Import |
| Mo | ppm | ~3% | Import |
| Ti | ppm | ~1% | Import |
| Al | not native metal | ~0.5% | Import |
| Co | ~0.5% | residual in some alloys | Useful, dilute |
| W, Ta, Re, Hf | traces / none | SX / 230 / 247 | Do not plan plates around them |

---

## 9. Short spec language (copy onto a title block)

- Grade A: slagged Fe–Ni, named by heat and Ni%.
- Grade B: name a real Fe–Ni alloy (A-286 or 800) only after Cr assay exists.
- Grade C: name 600 / 625 / 718 only after Ni concentrate + alloy book exist.
- No single-crystal, no Re, no “Psyche-718.”
- Superalloy is the face or the cup. Hemp or metal foam is the core. The exo is still the skeleton.